Subject: Re: Post-call recap + next steps (integration + rate limits)

Priya — great questions, answered inline: 

1) Idempotency TTL: we can extend persisted idempotency records to 72h for enterprise Dedicated/Private customers (configurable). For hosted customers the default is 24h, but we can support a longer window for Acme under a dedicated contract. If you provide your own token we will honor it and store the mapping server-side.

2) Streaming resume: current SDKs do not resume an interrupted token stream out-of-the-box. Recommended patterns: 
   - For UI assistant sessions, use per-session requestIds and checkpoint the last confirmed token index in your client. On retry, ask the model to continue from that point using structured tool-calling (stateful handoff).
   - For more robust resume, we recommend using short polling with chunked responses or storing interim state in your app and asking the model to output only the delta.

3) Quotas per-route: yes — we expose quotas at the route/model level. Headers include X-Model-RateLimit-Limit and X-Model-RateLimit-Remaining so your router can decide to fallback to a cheaper variant. SDK will expose a helper to read these headers and implement an automatic fallback callback.

Also sharing a small retry pseudocode we usually recommend:

  function callWithRetries(request) {
    let attempt = 0;
    const maxAttempts = 5;
    while (attempt < maxAttempts) {
      try {
        const res = await send(request);
        if (res.status === 200) return res;
        if (res.status === 429 || res.status === 503) {
          const retryAfter = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
          const backoff = Math.min(8000, (2 ** attempt) * 200);
          const jitter = Math.random() * backoff;
          await sleep(retryAfter ? retryAfter * 1000 : jitter);
          attempt++;
          continue;
        }
        // non-retriable 4xx other than 429
        throw new Error(`Non-retriable status ${res.status}`);
      } catch (err) {
        if (attempt >= maxAttempts - 1) throw err;
        await sleep(Math.random() * 200 * (2 ** attempt));
        attempt++;
      }
    }
  }

Happy to demo this on the call — I’ll bring a short notebook showing backoff behavior vs. burst traffic.

